  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nCreating command invoker/target relationships without requiring IDs.\nCommands enable a really nice abstraction for linking between elements, however it relies on the ID mechanism, creating a burden of having to create and maintain these IDs.\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\nGenerating IDs with a framework or general store using JS\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\nAllow some form of implicit resolution of command target based on the command type.\n\nFor example, the following button can close the dialog:\n```html\n<dialog>\n  <button command=close>x</button>\n</dialog>\n```\n\nAn attribute (?) or element types (?) can scope a particular component as such:\n```html\n<section commandscope>\n  <button command=play>\n  <video>\n</section>\n```\n\nThe above would link the \"play\" command to the first element in the nearest commandscope that supports the `play` command.\n\n\n### Anything else?\n\nThis is derived from an effort to make IDREFs more manageable and/or give them more powers. There was a long discussion about this at #10143 but this particular proposal/issue is much more limited in scope.\n\n//cc @lukewarlow @nt1m @keithamus @leaverou",
